  <prompt>
    Add Jest tests for four fragile client helpers in Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components that shipped without coverage: NarrativeCitedText.buildSegments (segment splitter, @107), useBriefingRender.isEmptyResponse (@60), useInlineTodoCreate (primary-contact wiring hook), and HighPrioritySection.actionToBadge (@158) + reasonToLabel (@213). Cover edge cases including empty input, missing itemId, and malformed segments. Per FR-C6. NOTE: the R7 note referenced a helper named classifyDueDate that does NOT exist — do not write tests for it; the real HighPrioritySection helpers are actionToBadge/reasonToLabel.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in Jest + React Testing Library, the Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components test conventions, and Fluent v9 client helpers.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Jest test files exist at the repo's KEEP test path (src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/) for all four helpers — buildSegments, isEmptyResponse, useInlineTodoCreate, and actionToBadge + reasonToLabel — each covering the happy path plus the named edge cases. No test references a non-existent classifyDueDate. All new tests pass under the existing jest runner.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R7 W12 shipped these helpers without tests (notes/inbound-from-r7/03 item 2). buildSegments is a regex-based inline-citation segment splitter (regression-prone); isEmptyResponse decides the "no data" render state (partial-data edge cases); useInlineTodoCreate wires retrieveMultipleRecords → sprk_AssignedTo@odata.bind (failure paths untested); actionToBadge/reasonToLabel map High-Priority action/reason enums to badges/labels. The R7 note mislabeled the date classifier as classifyDueDate — the actual client helpers are actionToBadge/reasonToLabel/formatShortDate/formatRelative; the date classifier lives server-side as ClassifyAction and is out of scope here.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/components/NarrativeCitedText.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/hooks/useBriefingRender.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/hooks/useInlineTodoCreate.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/components/HighPrioritySection.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/inbound-from-r7/03-code-review-followups.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Test ONLY these four surfaces: NarrativeCitedText.buildSegments (@107), useBriefingRender.isEmptyResponse (@60), useInlineTodoCreate (the primary-contact wiring hook), HighPrioritySection.actionToBadge (@158) + reasonToLabel (@213). Do NOT author a test for classifyDueDate — it does not exist in the codebase; the R7 note's name was wrong.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">New test files land at the repo's existing KEEP path src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/ using the existing naming convention (*.test.ts / *.test.tsx), mirroring existing tests there (e.g. NarrativeBullet.test.tsx, useBriefingActions.test.ts). Do NOT create a new __tests__/ directory.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Required edge cases: buildSegments → empty input string, malformed/overlapping segment, a segment with a missing/unresolvable itemId. isEmptyResponse → fully-empty response AND partial-data present. useInlineTodoCreate → a createTodo path where the primary-contact lookup returns no record (missing itemId / no contact) and the failure path. actionToBadge/reasonToLabel → each mapped enum value plus an unknown/undefined value falling back safely.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">New tests land at KEEP paths and follow the test-shape rules (no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;-equivalent anti-patterns; test observable behavior of the helpers, not implementation trivia). These are MAINTAIN-class unit tests for shipped, non-trivial logic.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT modify the production helper files — this task adds tests only. If a helper is untestable as written (e.g. not exported), the minimum change is exporting it; note any such change explicitly.</constraint>
  </constraints>

