        Mirror the setup/mocking style of the existing tests in this folder (NarrativeBullet.test.tsx for components, useBriefingActions.test.ts / useInlineTodoCreate.computeDueDate.test.ts for hooks) — same import paths, render/renderHook helpers, and mock conventions.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the four helpers to enumerate their branches and public signatures: buildSegments (NarrativeCitedText.tsx:107), isEmptyResponse (useBriefingRender.ts:60), useInlineTodoCreate.ts, actionToBadge (HighPrioritySection.tsx:158) + reasonToLabel (HighPrioritySection.tsx:213). Confirm which are exported; note any needing an export.</step>
    <step order="2">Read 1-2 existing tests in the test/ folder to match the runner config, imports, and mock style.</step>
    <step order="3">Write test/NarrativeCitedText.buildSegments.test.ts (or .tsx) covering happy path + empty input + malformed/overlapping segment + missing itemId.</step>
    <step order="4">Write test/useBriefingRender.isEmptyResponse.test.ts covering empty response + partial-data-present.</step>
    <step order="5">Write test/useInlineTodoCreate.test.ts (renderHook) covering the primary-contact resolve path, the no-record/missing-itemId path, and the failure path — mocking retrieveMultipleRecords.</step>
    <step order="6">Write test/HighPrioritySection.badges.test.ts covering each actionToBadge and reasonToLabel mapped value plus an unknown/undefined fallback.</step>
    <step order="7">Run the jest suite for the package; confirm all new tests pass and no test targets classifyDueDate.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md task 035 → completed; record any deviations (incl. any export-only production change) in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

