  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Jest tests exist at the KEEP path (src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/) for buildSegments, isEmptyResponse, useInlineTodoCreate, and actionToBadge + reasonToLabel.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">buildSegments tests cover empty input, a malformed/overlapping segment, and a segment with a missing/unresolvable itemId; all pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">isEmptyResponse tests cover the fully-empty response AND a partial-data-present case; both pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">useInlineTodoCreate tests cover the primary-contact resolve path, a no-record/missing-itemId path, and a failure path (retrieveMultipleRecords mocked); all pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">actionToBadge and reasonToLabel tests cover each mapped enum value plus an unknown/undefined value that falls back safely; all pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No test file references classifyDueDate; the jest suite for the package passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No production helper file is modified except (if strictly necessary) adding an export, which is noted in notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    See spec.md FR-C6, plan.md Phase B.6, notes/inbound-from-r7/03 item 2. The R7 note's classifyDueDate is a naming error — corrected here to actionToBadge/reasonToLabel per the verified code map. Test folder is test/ (not __tests__/). Existing companion test useInlineTodoCreate.computeDueDate.test.ts shows the hook's test style.
